<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?>
<!--
  A copy of Southwind's user-asset file (old/Southwind.Terminal/Toolbar.xml — Southwind's ImportToolbar
  step: UserAssetsImporter.Preview + Import), imported here by `terminal import-assets`. Renamed
  UserAssets.xml because it carries every user asset, not just the toolbars: 10 UserCharts, 2 UserQueries,
  the example Dashboard, 7 ToolbarMenus and the side Toolbar.

  Kept as close to the original as possible — same guids (the guid IS the asset's identity, so a re-import
  overwrites the same rows), same order, same attributes. Every edit is marked with an `altea:` comment;
  elements for features this port does not have are COMMENTED OUT rather than deleted, so re-syncing with
  Signum stays a diff.

  The systematic edits (documented divergences, see CLAUDE.md):
   * TOKENS ARE ROOTLESS. A token is spelled exactly as Signum spells it (PascalCase) except that there is
     no "Entity." prefix, altea's query root being the entity itself: Signum's
     "Entity.Details.Element.Product" is "Details.Element.Product", and "Entity.TotalPrice.Sum" is
     "TotalPrice.Sum". Reading one back tolerates either case, and LEGACY MODE also drops a stored
     "Entity." — so this file is the only place the prefix has to be taken off by hand.
   * The SmartDateTime grammar ("-1/mm/dd 00:00:00", "yyyy/mm/01 00:00:00") IS ported — see
     @altea/altea-user-assets data/FilterValueConverters — so those date filters are live, verbatim.
   * There is no storable spelling for the ROOT (entity) token: its key is "" and QueryTokenEmbedded.
     tokenString has StringLengthValidator(min 1). Where Signum wrote Token="Entity" this uses "ToString",
     and the Dashboard's TokenEquivalenceGroup (which needs Product's root token) is commented out.
   * `Owner` is preserved verbatim but currently IGNORED: UserAssetsImportExport.parseLiteKey is a stub, so
     every imported asset lands GLOBAL (owner null) — visible to every role.
   * Signum.Workflow / Signum.Map / Signum.Cache / Signum.Eval / Signum.Translation / Signum.Help are not
     ported, and Signum.Word became @altea/altea-office-template (WordTemplate -> OfficeTemplate).
-->
